* The pump phase now starts earlier (`h < 0.9`) and continues until the height is safely above the termination threshold, giving the system more time to accumulate kinetic energy.  
* The dump phase is triggered only after the height exceeds `1.1`, preventing premature braking that previously caused the swing to stall near `h ≈ 1.0`.  
