* The safety cut‑offs are low enough to intervene before the swing‑up overshoots and crashes, yet high enough not to interfere with the normal pump‑up.  
* The first‑link stabiliser is kept but with a larger angle threshold (0.6 rad) so it only activates when truly needed, reducing unnecessary torque that would waste steps.

