## 2. What assumptions were right / wrong  

| Assumption | Verdict | Evidence |
|------------|---------|----------|
| **A1 – High angular velocity is dangerous → stop the motor** | **Wrong** for this task. | The swing‑up needs *large* angular velocities (|ω| ≈ 5–8 rad/s).  Stopping the motor when `|ω|>8` (first strategy) or `>20` (second) kills the swing‑up before it can succeed. |
