2. **Uses both angular position and velocity** of the second joint (θ₂, ω₂) – the first joint is fixed, so controlling ω₂ is enough to stabilise the tip.
3. **Limits torque magnitude** to avoid the abrupt flips that caused the PD overshoot (e.g. clamp the control signal to `[-0.2, 0.2]` → map to discrete actions 0/2, otherwise 1).

